# Live site must stay snappy (Oct 2026 outage lesson)

Owner lesson (**Oct 2026**): `/tl` slim+hydrate, InstantBrowse `ranking_bulk` warm, full-timeline vote bootstrap, and full-viewport `backdrop-filter` put **production** in a state where browse/detail felt dead. Getting back to usable took days. **Do not repeat.**

## Hard rule

1. **Never deploy a change that makes the live homepage / browse / detail / `/tl` feel laggy** relative to the snappy-static-cache bar — even if the feature is “correct” or “temporary.”
2. **Feature-complete ≠ cold multi-second API.** Keep full payloads when needed; **prewarm** (server) + light **hover prefetch** (client). Do **not** invent scroll/IO hydrate storms or site-wide megabyte fetches to “fix” size.
3. **No full-viewport `backdrop-filter: blur`** on detail / search / compare overlays (or sticky header glass). Solid wash only — blur tanks GPU the moment the overlay appears.
4. **No auto `ranking_bulk` / InstantBrowse catalog warm** on idle after first paint. Arm only on explicit search focus (or equivalent user intent).
5. **Do not fetch full `/api/banner_timeline` from site-wide notices.** Votes use `vote_pools` only.
6. **Teko is Latin HUD only.** Never put Teko (or `text-transform:uppercase` via Teko stacks) on game names — Greek `ν` becomes `N`. Keep `unicode-range` Latin on Teko; names/titles use `--font-body`.
7. Before claiming live is OK: rebuild `app.min.js` + shell CSS when touched, restart local Flask for Python, hard-refresh, and say **local vs live** honestly (`verify-live-before-fixed.mdc`).

## Forbidden “perf” patterns (caused the outage)

| Pattern | Why it killed the site |
|---|---|
| Slim `/tl` + IntersectionObserver hydrate | Scroll storms + jank; worse than full warm payload |
| Idle `ranking_bulk` ~1MB warm | GIL + main-thread freeze ~8–15s after “good” first paint |
| Full timeline in content-notice bootstrap | Races browse/detail on every cold load |
| Overlay / sticky `backdrop-filter` | Solid wash moment = GPU thrash |
| Shipping `app.js` without minify/verify | Live serves `app.min.js` |

## Allowed recovery patterns (what restored snappy)

- Full featured `/tl` JSON **with** server prewarm after browse caches + nav hover/`pointerdown` prefetch
- **`/tl` `/new` `/ip` spinner bar (Oct 2026 — owner-confirmed)** — keep this class forever:
  - Early head fetch on deep-link (`/tl`, `/new`, `/ip`): start the tab’s API **during** HTML/CSS/JS download
  - Session soft paint + background refresh where the payload is small (`/tl`)
  - Delayed spinner (~100ms) **only** on empty cold tab panels — never when replacing visible content with a different entity
  - Unit/char/supporter detail: on switch (close→other or browse another), **immediately** clear to spinner — never leave the previous dossier on screen
  - Nav `pointerenter`/`pointerdown` prefetch for `/tl`, `/new`, `/ip`
  - Idle low-priority prefetch of **timeline only** (~37KB gzip) after browse first paint — **not** idle `ranking_bulk`, **not** idle `/api/sp_investment` (~1.4MB; races `/u` detail)
  - **never** `JSON.stringify` the full timeline into `sessionStorage` from that idle path; defer session write to idle from `/tl` load only; skip/defer while detail modal is open (timeout ≥8–12s)
- Pin timeline cache keys so eviction does not force cold rebuild under traffic
- Pre-serialized raw+gzip bodies for large warm JSON (`/tl`, published `/tm` `/dm`) — no re-jsonify under GIL
- Published matrix gzip served as bytes (never keep decoded multi‑MB boards in `_api_cache`)
- Cap refillable MSY pair cache so RSS stays under ~1GB (default 12k, not 50k)
- Gate deferred work behind detail-closed + long idle / user intent
- Remove FX/decoration that burns bandwidth without product value (e.g. pedestal area spirals)

## Site-wide bar (not one tab)

When any tab feels below bar, **measure the whole critical path** before patching that tab alone:
`/health` · `/` · `/api/characters` · `/api/units` · `/api/banner_timeline` · `/api/tag_matrix` · `/api/debuff_matrix` · collections catalog.
If `/health` alone is multi-hundred-ms while RSS ≥ ~1.1GB, fix **process pressure** (RAM / re-serialize / prewarm) — do not only slim the reported page.

After **any** new feature or “perf” change, `/tl` must still meet the spinner bar above (deep-link + tab switch + revisit) with **no look/feature change**. Same class for other heavy tabs when adding similar loads: overlap fetch with boot, session soft paint, delayed spinner — never regress to a cold spinner on every open.

## Checklist before push to Railway

- [ ] Cold `/` + open unit/char detail still feels instant locally
- [ ] `/tl` deep-link / tab open: **no spinner** when early boot, session cache, or prefetch already has data (delayed spinner only on true cold miss); warm API still &lt; ~100ms after server prewarm
- [ ] No new idle megabyte fetches; no new full-viewport blur
- [ ] No new boot-prewarm of multi‑MB boards (`/tm` `/dm`) into pinned API cache
- [ ] Live `/health` `memory.rss_mb` not climbing past ~1GB after “perf” deploys
- [ ] `node scripts/verify_app_js_bundle.mjs` if `app.js` changed
- [ ] Honest status: local-only vs needs deploy

If a change needs a trade-off that risks live snappiness, **stop and tell the owner** before shipping — do not “try it on Railway.”
